   "2018-12-06",
   "2018-12-06"
  ]
 },
 "method": {
  "rules": {
   "cellM": 0.5,
   "minAreaM2": 6,
   "lakeReachM2": 1,
   "drawnShareMax": 0.25,
   "drawnMarginM": 1,
   "pieceMinM2": 6,
   "pieceMinWidthM": 1.5,
   "pieceLakeMin": 0.5,
   "ringM": 3,
   "ringReadMin": 0.5,
   "ringWaterMin": 0.75
  },
  "roofs": "Building (class 6) returns, moved into the town frame by the outline registration (-0.04, 0.84) m and binned in 0.5 m cells; cells holding them join eight ways into roofs, over land and water alike. A roof is kept when at least 1 m² of it lies in Lake Dora's OSM outline, and at most 25% of it inside an outline the game draws (OSM and county buildings, the generator's structures). A roof joined to a drawn one beyond that share is that building's own (a wing, a porch, an attached boathouse its county sketch leaves out) and is not kept.",
  "outline": "Cells within 1 m of a drawn outline are left to it. The rest of a roof splits into parts that join eight ways; a part of 6 m² or more is outlined by rectangles in its own frame (pieces): the smallest rectangle around it, unless that roofs over an open rectangle of 6 m², 1.5 m wide, its cells (closed by a 3 x 3 square) do not fill; otherwise the largest rectangles its cells fill, one after another, in the frame where the largest is biggest, while one of that size remains. A piece stands over water where 50% of it lies in the lake's outline, or where the lidar sees water around it: 50% of the cells within 3 m read as water or ground (no roof over them) and 75% of those read as water (water returns, or none at all); the rest (onLand) are left out.",
  "heights": "Per piece, from its own returns, in metres above the lake's lidar level: the eave from the roof planes as in lidar-roofs.json (the 25th percentile where none is found), the ridge at the 98th percentile; form and pitch by the same rules (roofs.mjs)."
 },
